/**
* The interface used in an {@link yfiles.IGraph} implementation to control the layout of {@link yfiles.IEdge edges}.
* This interface provides read-only access to the properties of a bend. In order to modify the state of an instance use
* the various methods provided by the {@link yfiles.IGraph} this instance belongs to. Bends are stored in {@link yfiles.IListEnumerable}s, that can be
* obtained from the {@link yfiles.IEdge} implementation that owns this bend. Like all items in an `IGraph`, this item supports
* the {@link yfiles.ILookup.lookup} method that can be used to query additional aspects of the item.
*
*
* __Working with a bend in the graph__
* ```
* const graph = graphComponent.graph
* const node1 = graph.createNodeAt(new Point(0, 0))
* const node2 = graph.createNodeAt(new Point(100, 0))
* const edge = graph.createEdge(node1, node2)
*
* // add a bend to the edge
* const bend = graph.addBend(edge, new Point(50, 20))
*
* // the newly created bend is part of the graph
* console.log(graph.contains(bend)) // true
*
* // the bend belongs to its owner
* console.log(bend.owner === edge) // true
* console.log(edge.bends.size) // 1
* console.log(edge.bends.get(0) === bend) // true
*
* // removing the bend removes it from the graph
* graph.remove(bend)
* console.log(graph.contains(bend)) // false
* // and from its owner
* console.log(bend.owner === null) // true
* console.log(edge.bends.size) // 0
* ```
*
*
* __Bends cannot live without an owner in the graph__
* ```
* console.log(graph.contains(bend)) // true
* graph.remove(bend.owner)
* console.log(graph.contains(bend)) // false
* ```
*
* [Read this documentation with sample code online](https://docs.yworks.com/yfileshtml/#/api/IBend).
*
* The graph model with all relevant types and their relationships is presented in detail in the section [The Graph Model](https://docs.yworks.com/yfileshtml/#/dguide/graph).
*
* Using the look-up mechanism is explained in the section [Service Locator Pattern: Lookup](https://docs.yworks.com/yfileshtml/#/dguide/customizing_concepts_lookup).
*/
