/**
* Method to adjust the size of a group node.
* This will resize the group node bounds such that the node requires the least amount of space. If the node does not have
* any {@link yfiles.IGraph.getChildren children} its bounds will be left unchanged. This will also respect any {@link yfiles.INodeSizeConstraintProvider}s for
* {@link yfiles.INode}s, that are available in the lookup of the `groupNode`.
*
*
* __How to create create a group node with children__
* ```
* // create a group node
* const group = graph.createGroupNode()
* // add some child nodes
* graph.createNode(group, new Rect(10, 10, 30, 30))
* graph.createNode(group, new Rect(50, 10, 30, 30))
* graph.createNode(group, new Rect(50, 50, 30, 30))
* // adjust the group node's layout to include all its children
* graph.adjustGroupNodeLayout(group)
* ```
*
* `AdjustGroupNodeLayout` only affects the node it is called for. To properly adjust all of its ancestors, too, one has to
* adjust all of them from the given node to the root:
* ```
* for (const nodeToAdjust of graph.groupingSupport.getPathToRoot(
*   innermostGroup
* )) {
*   graph.adjustGroupNodeLayout(nodeToAdjust)
* }
* ```
*
* [Read this documentation online](https://docs.yworks.com/yfileshtml/#/api/IGraph%23adjustGroupNodeLayout(INode)).
*
* @param groupNode The group node to adjust the size of.
* @throws {@link yfiles.Exception} __(ArgumentError)__ `groupNode` is not in this graph.
* @see {@link yfiles.IGroupBoundsCalculator}
* @see {@link yfiles.INodeSizeConstraintProvider}
* @see {@link yfiles.GroupingSupport.calculateMinimumEnclosedArea}
* @see {@link yfiles.GroupingSupport.enlargeGroupNode}
* @see {@link yfiles.GroupingSupport.enlargeAllGroupNodes}
*/
adjustGroupNodeLayout(groupNode: yfiles.INode): void;
