/**
Node labeling policies defining how node labels are placed by the integrated node labeling mechanism of algorithms
{@link yfiles.BalloonLayout}, {@link yfiles.CactusGroupLayout}, {@link yfiles.CircularLayout} and
{@link yfiles.RadialLayout}.
@see {@link yfiles.CircularLayout.nodeLabelingPolicy}
@see {@link yfiles.CompactDiskLayout.nodeLabelingPolicy}
@see {@link yfiles.CactusGroupLayout.nodeLabelingPolicy}
@see {@link yfiles.RadialLayout.nodeLabelingPolicy}
@see {@link yfiles.BalloonLayout.nodeLabelingPolicy}
@final*/
export enum NodeLabelingPolicy {
/**
Node labeling policy for ray-like label placement at nodes with zero or one child node or nodes that are placed on the
perimeter of a circular component.
Labels belonging to nodes with zero or exactly one successor (thus forming a sort of chain) will not be oriented
horizontal but ray-like; they get the same orientation as their nodes' incoming edge. For the circular layout, nodes
that are placed on the perimeter of a circular component and have neighbors connected only to this component will also
be placed ray-like. The labels of the other nodes will be oriented horizontally and placed at the center of the
corresponding node.
{@link yfiles.BalloonLayout} places the label of nodes in the inner circles ray-like inside the nodes with the same
orientation as their nodes' incoming edge. {@link yfiles.RadialLayout} places these labels outside the nodes with the
same angle as the nodes.
{@link yfiles.CircularLayout} places the label of nodes that belong to the perimeter of a circle ray-like outside the
node with the same orientation as their nodes' incoming edge. If the partition style is {@link yfiles.CircularLayoutStyle.BCC_COMPACT}
or
{@link yfiles.CircularLayoutStyle.BCC_ISOLATED}, the labels of the nodes that are connected to more than one circular
components will be also placed horizontal, even if they are placed on the perimeter of the circle. Labels of nodes that
belong on a chain will be placed ray-like but inside the node with the same orientation as their nodes' incoming edge.
{@link yfiles.CactusGroupLayout} places the labels of inner nodes ray-like inside the nodes with the same orientation as
their placement relative to their parent node. The labels of leaves are placed outside the nodes with the same angle as
the leaves' placement relative to their parent node.
[Read this documentation online](https://docs.yworks.com/yfileshtml/#/api/NodeLabelingPolicy%23RAY_LIKE).*/
RAY_LIKE,
/**
Node labeling policy for ray-like label placement at nodes with zero children or nodes that are placed on the perimeter
of a circular component.
{@link yfiles.BalloonLayout} places the labels corresponding to leaf nodes outside the node (without overlaps) with the
same orientation as their nodes' incoming edge. {@link yfiles.RadialLayout} places these labels also outside the nodes
with the same angle as the nodes. {@link yfiles.CircularLayout} places the label of nodes with no children or of nodes
that belong to the perimeter of a circle and have neighbors at the same circle ray-like outside the node with the same
orientation as their nodes' incoming edge. The labels of the other nodes will be oriented horizontally and placed at the
center of the corresponding node.
{@link yfiles.CactusGroupLayout} places the labels of inner nodes horizontally at the center of the corresponding node.
The labels of leaves are placed outside the nodes with the same angle as the leaves' placement relative to their parent
node.*/
RAY_LIKE_LEAVES,
/**
Node labeling policy for horizontal label placement at all nodes.
The node labels are placed at the center of the corresponding node.*/
HORIZONTAL
}
