/**
@see {@link yfiles.TabularLayout.layoutPolicy}
@final*/
export enum TabularLayoutPolicy {
/**
Layout policy that automatically chooses the table size of the layout.
The resulting table gets a dimension such that both row count and column count are similar, leading to a maximally
square table with respect to the row and column count (actual node sizes are not considered). For example, given a graph
with 14 nodes, a 4x4 grid will be created.
The nodes are arranged in the table in a row-wise fashion using the order provided by {@link yfiles.TabularLayout.nodeComparer}. If {@link yfiles.TabularLayout.nodeComparer} is `null` and {@link yfiles.TabularLayout.considerEdges} is enabled, the
algorithm applies a heuristic approach that leads to an arrangement of the nodes that has a low overall edge length.
__Warning:__ If a {@link yfiles.PartitionGrid} instance is registered that already contains {@link yfiles.PartitionGrid.rows rows} and/or {@link yfiles.PartitionGrid.columns columns}, the number of
rows/columns is ignored and, furthermore, the list of rows will be
_cleared_. However, the settings of the first row and the first column are used as template for the settings of the newly created
rows and columns.
@see {@link yfiles.TabularLayout.layoutPolicy}*/
AUTO_SIZE,
/**
Layout policy that adopts the size from an already registered {@link yfiles.PartitionGrid} instance.
The algorithm generates a tabular layout with the number of {@link yfiles.PartitionGrid.rows rows} and {@link yfiles.PartitionGrid.columns columns} as specified by the registered grid
instance. The settings of the respective {@link yfiles.RowDescriptor}s and
{@link yfiles.ColumnDescriptor}s are considered.
Using this layout policy, it is possible to exactly define in which cell of the table a certain node should be placed by
mapping a specific {@link yfiles.PartitionCellId} to a node. {@link yfiles.PartitionCellId} instances can be created using
methods {@link yfiles.PartitionGrid.createCellId} and {@link yfiles.PartitionGrid.createCellId}. Multi-cells (see e.g.
{@link yfiles.PartitionGrid.createCellSpanId}) are not allowed. The node-cell mapping must be defined in a {@link yfiles.IDataProvider}
registered with the graph with key {@link yfiles.PartitionGrid.PARTITION_CELL_ID_DP_KEY}.
Nodes without a specific mapping to a cell are inserted one after another in a row-wise manner in the order defined by
the specified {@link yfiles.TabularLayout.nodeComparer}. If {@link yfiles.TabularLayout.nodeComparer} is `null` and {@link yfiles.TabularLayout.considerEdges} is enabled, the algorithm applies a heuristic approach that leads to an arrangement of
these nodes that has a low overall edge length.
__Warning:__ The registered {@link yfiles.PartitionGrid} instance must be large enough for all nodes to fit into the grid. Otherwise,
a {@link yfiles.Exception InvalidGraphStructureError} exception will be thrown.
[Read this documentation online](https://docs.yworks.com/yfileshtml/#/api/TabularLayoutPolicy%23FIXED_SIZE).
@see {@link yfiles.TabularLayout.layoutPolicy}*/
FIXED_SIZE,
/**
Layout policy that uses the coordinates of the input graph to determine the table size and the mapping of the nodes to
the cells.
Enabling this feature, the current layout of the input graph will be interpreted as a sketch for the layout algorithm.
Nodes are assigned to the same row if there exists a horizontal line that crosses through both of their bounding boxes.
Similarly, nodes are assigned to the same column if there exists a vertical line that crosses through both of their
bounding boxes. Clearly, this strategy only works smoothly if the given input already resembles a rough table
arrangement.
If the given layout does not offer any division of the nodes into column and rows or contains overlapping nodes, then
the sketch is ambiguous and the algorithm will chose one valid variant.
__Warning:__ If a {@link yfiles.PartitionGrid} instance is registered that already contains {@link yfiles.PartitionGrid.rows rows} and/or {@link yfiles.PartitionGrid.columns columns}, the number of
rows/columns is ignored and, furthermore, the list of rows will be
_cleared_. However, the settings of the first row and the first column are used as template for the settings of the newly created
rows and columns.
@see {@link yfiles.TabularLayout.layoutPolicy}*/
FROM_SKETCH
}
