/**
Gets or sets the maximum allowed error for the fitting process.
The error is defined as the minimum distance between an original input control point (i.e. bend) of and edge and the
fitted bezier curve.
The maximum error must be greater than or equal to zero.
## Note
It is not recommended to set the maximum error to really small values, e.g., zero or one. Doing so produces a high
number of bezier pieces and, thus, a high number of control points for each edge.
@throws {@link yfiles.Exception} __(ArgumentError)__ if the specified maximum error is negative
@type {number}*/
