/**
Gets or sets the original, non-expanded bounds of the {@link yfiles.ClearAreaLayoutData.expandedNode}.
When an expanded node is provided, the area that must be cleared is directly derived from the bounds of the expanded
node. The original, non-expanded (smaller) bounds of the expanded node are helpful to preserve the mental map of the
overall drawing to a higher degree than without the additional knowledge about the previous layout. Note, however, that
only strategies {@link yfiles.ClearAreaStrategy.PRESERVE_SHAPES}, {@link yfiles.ClearAreaStrategy.PRESERVE_SHAPES_UNIFORM}
and {@link yfiles.ClearAreaStrategy.GLOBAL} will significantly profit from it.
@see {@link yfiles.ClearAreaLayoutData.expandedNode}
@see {@link yfiles.ClearAreaLayoutData.expandedNodeOriginalEdgePaths}
@see {@link yfiles.ClearAreaLayout.EXPANDED_NODE_ORIGINAL_BOUNDS_DP_KEY}*/
